gaps.proposedFix:
Add a raw-bytes field, width literal or expression, producing ProtoValue.Bytes:
{ "bytes": 32, "as": "random" }
{ "bytes": "capture.sessionIdLen", "as": "sessionId" }
{ "bytes": "rest", "as": "body" }        // to the end of the enclosing span
In encode mode `{"bytes":32,"value":"inputs.random | unhex"}` additionally asserts the width, which fixes gap 12 for free.

Add span-relative position functions usable in `when:`: `remaining(group:X)`, `consumed(group:X)`, `offset()`. Then:
{ "group":"exts", "when":"remaining(group:chBody) > 0", "fields":[ … ] }
Decode-mode groups must therefore carry a byte extent, taken from the length field that precedes them: { "group":"chBody", "extent":"capture.hsLength", "fields":[ … ] }. That extent is also what makes `overBytes` (gap 1) and bounded sub-parse checkable.

Scope group names to the enclosing iteration and resolve span references innermost-first, so len(group:item) inside `each` means this iteration's instance:
{ "each":"inputs.certs", "as":"c", "fields":[ {"u24be":"len(group:item)"}, {"group":"item","fields":[ {"value":"c | unhex"} ]} ] }
A reference that escapes an iteration (naming a group from a different iteration) becomes a validation error, keeping the acyclicity guarantee intact.

Add a bitwise-and to the expression language and an `ignoreIf` on a field:
{ "u16be":null, "as":"type", "ignoreIf":"(value & 0x0f0f) == 0x0a0a" }
Ignored items are still consumed and still preserved for re-encode; they are merely excluded from semantic matching such as the `negotiates` membership check.

Require an explicit anchor and make bare `start` a validation error inside a nested group:
{ "checksum": { "alg":"crc16/modbus", "over":"from:group:record.start to:here", "as":"u16le" } }
Same anchoring syntax as len(group:X), so span references have exactly one resolution rule everywhere.
